/* TUTORIAL */

:: TutorialStart
<div class="tutorial-panel"><div class="tutorial-icon">🎓</div>
    <h2>Welcome to the Tutorial!</h2><p>Hi, explorer! Ruby here! 👋</p><p>I'll show you how to explore Vascular Village and complete activities about the human body.</p><p>You'll learn how to choose an activity, understand answer choices, read feedback, and discover what you've learned.</p><p><strong>Don't worry! You won't need to answer any questions during this tutorial.</strong></p><p>Ready? Let's get started!</p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "Continue →">><<goto "TutorialMission">><</button>></div>
</div>


/* should show the populated menu page, maybe just a popup window at the bottom of the screen to explain how the game works */
:: TutorialMission
<div class="tutorial-panel"><h3>Step 1: Choose Your Adventure</h3><p>On the home screen, you'll find five areas to explore:</p><ul>
        <li>🧠 Brain</li>
        <li>🩸 Blood Cells</li>
        <li>❤️ Heart</li>
        <li>🩸 Blood Vessels</li>
        <li>🫁 Lungs</li></ul><p>Each area teaches you something different about the human body and how to keep it healthy.</p><p>When you choose an area, you'll enter its activity menu. This is where you can explore the available activities.</p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "Continue →">><<goto "TutorialChoices">><</button>></div>
</div>

/* again, should show a popup window at the bottom of the screen to explain the choices */
:: TutorialChoices
<div class="tutorial-panel"><h3>Step 2: Explore an Activity</h3><p>Each body system has activities designed to help you learn through questions.</p><p>When you select an activity, it opens on its own screen.</p><p>Depending on the activity, you might need to:</p><ul>
        <li>🔎 Read a question or scenario.</li>
        <li>💭 Think about what you already know.</li>
        <li>👆 Select an answer or make a choice.</li>
    </ul><p>Some activities may work differently from others, so always read the instructions shown on the screen.</p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "Continue →">><<goto "TutorialFeedback">><</button>></div>
</div>


/* popup window at the bottom of screen to explain feedback */
/* should have button with "Return Home" to finish tutorial */
:: TutorialFeedback
<div class="tutorial-panel"><h3>Step 3: Learn from Feedback</h3><p>After making a choice in an activity, you may receive feedback explaining the result.</p><p>Feedback helps you understand:</p><ul>
        <li>✅ What you got right.</li>
        <li>💡 Why an answer makes sense.</li>
        <li>🧠 Important facts about the human body.</li>
        <li>🌱 What you can learn from a mistake.</li></ul>
    <p>Don't be discouraged if you get something wrong! The goal is to learn, improve your understanding, and discover something new.</p><p><strong>Take your time and read the feedback before moving on.</strong></p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "Continue →">><<goto "TutorialLesson">><</button>></div>
</div>

:: TutorialLesson
<div class="tutorial-panel"><h3>Step 4: Discover What You've Learned</h3><p>Completed activities include a lesson to help you understand the information you've discovered.</p><p>These lessons can help you connect what you've learned to everyday health.</p><p>For example, you might discover how exercise supports your heart or why your lungs need clean air.</p><p>Take a moment to think about what you've learned and how you could use that knowledge in your daily life.</p><p><strong>Every discovery brings you one step closer to becoming a health explorer!</strong></p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "Continue →">><<goto "TutorialComplete">><</button>></div>
</div>


:: TutorialComplete
<div class="tutorial-panel"><h2>You're Ready to Explore!</h2><p>Great job, explorer! 🎉</p><p>You now know how to navigate Vascular Village, open activities, understand answer choices, and learn from feedback.</p><p>Now it's time to put your knowledge into action!</p><p>Choose your favourite body system and begin your adventure with Ruby.</p><p><strong>Your journey to better health starts here!</strong></p><div class="tutorial-navigation"><<button "🏠 Return Home">><<goto "HomeScreen">><</button>></div>
</div>


